Yes — I’d make Reddit/community evidence a first-class input into the campus source ranking, because official university pages systematically over-surface the biggest programs and under-surface the smaller rooms where students say the real builders are.

But I would use Reddit for “where should Scout look?”, not for “is this founder good?” A Reddit thread can tell us that Penn Labs or E@B is where strong builders cluster; it should not increase an individual founder’s score unless we find actual project evidence.

